<title>AUSTRALIA: RGC says tin output rises in third qtr.</title>
<headline>RGC says tin output rises in third qtr.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-04-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Base metals and mineral sands miner RGC Ltd said on Thursday that higher plant throughput and ore grade at its Renison Tin unit more than offset continued low recoveries in the third quarter to end-March 1997.</p>
<p>Production also continued to increase at PT Koba Tin in Indonesia as a dredge reached its design parameters.</p>
<p>Rutile production at RGC Mineral Sands rose in the first quarter, aided by improved recoveries at Eneabba in Western Australia.  </p>
<p>Production of synthetic rutile fell due to planned maintenance, while zircon production was lower due to lower grades and qualities at the Eneabba North strands.</p>
